Here is the commit message:
Check if player is in arena on food level change.

This commit fixes a bug.

During a food level change event, if the arena is running and the food level lock is enabled, we just need to also make sure that the given player is actually in the arena, otherwise it affects everyone on the server.

Here is the root cause:
The food level change event handler only checked whether the arena was running and whether the `lockFoodLevel` setting was enabled, without verifying whether the specific player triggering the event (`p`) was actually a participant in that arena. Since Bukkit's `FoodLevelChangeEvent` fires for any player on the server whose food level changes, this meant that as long as any arena was running with `lockFoodLevel` enabled, the event was cancelled for **all players server-wide**—including those not involved in the arena at all. The missing player-scope check (`arena.inArena(p)`) caused the food level lock to incorrectly leak its effect beyond the arena's participants to the entire server.

Here is the patch:

     public void onFoodLevelChange(FoodLevelChangeEvent event) {
         if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) {
             return;
         }

         Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();

         if (arena.isRunning()) {
-            if (lockFoodLevel) {
+            if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         } else {
             // Always locked in lobby/spec
             if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {
                 event.setCancelled(true);
             }
         }
     }



